    "---\n",
    "## 🎯 Section 1: Overview & Math\n",
    "\n",
    "**Support Vector Machines** find a hyperplane that separates classes with the **maximum margin** (distance between the hyperplane and closest data points called *support vectors*).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Primal Optimization Problem (Soft Margin)\n",
    "$$\\min_{w, b, \\xi} \\frac{1}{2} ||w||^2 + C \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\xi_i$$\n",
    "Subject to: $y^{(i)}(w^T x^{(i)} + b) \\ge 1 - \\xi_i, \\quad \\xi_i \\ge 0$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Hinge Loss\n",
    "$$L(w, b) = \\frac{1}{2} ||w||^2 + C \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\max(0, 1 - y^{(i)}(w^T x^{(i)} + b))$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Kernel Trick\n",
    "Replaces dot products $x^{(i)T} x^{(j)}$ with a kernel function $K(x^{(i)}, x^{(j)})$, mapping low-dimensional non-linear features into a high-dimensional feature space where they are linearly separable!\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Linear Kernel**: $K(x, z) = x^T z$\n",
    "- **Polynomial Kernel**: $K(x, z) = (x^T z + c)^d$\n",
    "- **Radial Basis Function (RBF / Gaussian)**: $K(x, z) = \\exp(-\\gamma ||x - z||^2)$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
