    "---\n",
    "## ❓ Section 4: Interview Questions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q1: What are Support Vectors?\n",
    "<details><summary>Click for answer</summary>\n",
    "\n",
    "Support vectors are the data points that lie closest to the decision boundary (on the margin boundary or misclassified). They are the critical elements of the dataset: if you remove all non-support vector data points, the learned decision boundary remains completely unchanged!\n",
    "</details>\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q2: What is the effect of the C and Gamma parameters in RBF SVM?\n",
    "<details><summary>Click for answer</summary>\n",
    "\n",
    "- **C (Regularization)**: Controls the tradeoff between smooth decision boundary and classifying training points correctly.\n",
    "  - High C: Low bias, High variance (risk of overfitting, small margin, strict penalty for misclassification).\n",
    "  - Low C: High bias, Low variance (larger margin, more misclassification tolerance).\n",
    "- **Gamma ($\gamma$)**: Defines how far the influence of a single training example reaches.\n",
    "  - High Gamma: High variance (complex, tight decision boundary around support vectors).\n",
    "  - Low Gamma: High bias (smooth, broad decision boundary).\n",
    "</details>"
   ]
